  <article class="reader"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>HaRav Shalom Arush <span class="au">shlit”a</span></h1>
    <div class="paper">
      <p>Rabbi Shalom Arush is the founder and Rosh Yeshiva of the <strong>Chut Shel Chessed</strong> institutions in Jerusalem, and one of the most beloved teachers of emuna in our generation. Through his books and his shiurim he has brought the light of Rebbe Nachman of Breslov to hundreds of thousands of people across the world.</p>
      <p>His signature work, <em>The Garden of Emuna</em>, has sold in the millions and been translated into more than a dozen languages. Its message is simple and life-changing: everything Hashem does is for the good, and a person who lives with that faith — and who speaks to Hashem in his own words each day — is never truly alone.</p>
      <p>His teaching returns again and again to a few living roots: <strong>emuna</strong> — faith in a loving Creator; <strong>hisbodedus</strong> — personal, spoken prayer; <strong>gratitude</strong> — saying thank you until the heart believes it; and <strong>joy</strong> — the joy of a Jew who knows Whose hands he is in.</p>
      <p>This hub was built by his students, in English, so that his Torah can reach every heart that is looking for it — gathered from across the world and set in order, room by room.</p>
    </div>
